# Real bin/fm-watch.sh on lab:fm-dead (bare shell). FM_PAUSE_RESURFACE_SECS=25 FM_STALE_ESCALATE_SECS=6 FM_POLL=1.
# Each WAKE is acknowledged with bin/fm-wake-drain.sh and the watcher is re-armed, as firstmate does.
t+  0s CREW appends: paused: awaiting the upstream release
t+  3s WAKE rc=0: signal: /tmp/fm-lab.3RSOfV/state/dead.status
t+  7s WAKE rc=0: stale: lab:fm-dead (paused 7s, awaiting external - declared pause, rechecked on a long cadence not a wedge; confirm the wait still holds)
t+  9s CREW appends: resolved [key=other]: unrelated phase completed
# expectation: the unrelated append causes no early stale wake and does not restart the 25s cadence (recheck due ~25s after the declaration/first alert)
t+ 12s WAKE rc=0: signal: /tmp/fm-lab.3RSOfV/state/dead.status
t+ 32s WAKE rc=0: stale: lab:fm-dead (paused 32s, awaiting external - declared pause, rechecked on a long cadence not a wedge; confirm the wait still holds)
t+ 34s CREW appends: resolved: upstream release landed
t+ 34s CREW appends: paused: awaiting the upstream release
# expectation: the identical re-declaration is a new declaration, so its first stale sight alerts at once instead of waiting 25s
t+ 37s WAKE rc=0: signal: /tmp/fm-lab.3RSOfV/state/dead.status
t+ 41s WAKE rc=0: stale: lab:fm-dead (paused 6s, awaiting external - declared pause, rechecked on a long cadence not a wedge; confirm the wait still holds)
# expectation: after that alert the re-declared pause is quiet again until its own cadence
t+ 55s watcher quiet for 12s (no wake)
